  "statement_html": "We have two differentiable functions \\(f\\) and \\(g\\),\twith values and derivatives shown in the following table.\t<table class=\"wimscenter wimsborder\">\t<tr><th>x</th><th>-3</th><th>-2</th><th>-1</th><th>0</th><th>1</th><th>2</th><th>3</th></tr>\t<tr><th>\\(f{\\left(x \\right)}\\)</th>\t<td>5</td><td>-12</td><td>-15</td><td>8</td><td>-7</td><td>-8</td><td>-8</td></tr>\t<tr><th>\\(f '(x)\\)</th>\t<td>-11</td><td>8</td><td>-12</td><td>6</td><td>8</td><td>13</td><td>2</td></tr>\t<tr><th>\\(g{\\left(x \\right)}\\)</th>\t<td>-3</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>-3</td><td>-3</td><td>-3</td><td>-2</td></tr>\t<tr><th>\\(g'(x)\\)</th>\t<td>-8</td><td>1</td><td>4</td><td>-15</td><td>2</td><td>-9</td><td>7</td></tr>\t</table>\tLet \\(h\\) be defined by \\(h{\\left(x \\right)} = f{\\left(g{\\left(x \\right)} \\right)}\\). Compute the derivative\t\\(h'(2)\\).\t<div class=\"oef-enterreply\">Enter your reply:</div><div class=\"oefnoembed\"><div class=\"oef-noembed-ligne\"><span class=\"oef-noembed-nom\"><label for=\"reply1\">\\(h'(2)\\)</label> = </span><span class=\"oef-input\" name=\"reply1\" data-size=\"14\"></span></div></div>",
